message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Reson: an open-source EMG binary switch pipeline"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yuan
    given-names: Jerald
    email: jeraldhu.yuan@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeraldhu-yuan/reson"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-06-10
keywords:
  - EMG
  - electromyography
  - assistive technology
  - accessibility
  - human-machine interface
  - binary switch
  - ESP32
abstract: >-
  Reson is an early-stage, open-source electromyography (EMG) binary
  switch pipeline built on low-cost hardware (ESP32 + AD8232). It
  provides serial ingestion, feature extraction, interval-labeled and
  prompted data collection, baseline model training, and a runtime
  that emits binary switch down/up events, intended as a click layer
  for assistive human-machine interfaces such as eye-tracking cursor
  systems.
